cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this project, please cite it."
title: "Reduced-Order Forecasting of Particle-Laden Flow Evolution"
authors:
  - family-names: Bainbridge
    given-names: Thomas
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ThomasBainbridge/Reduced-Order-Particle-Flow"
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - inertial particles
  - preferential concentration
  - reduced-order modelling
  - dynamic mode decomposition
  - scientific machine learning
  - PyTorch
abstract: >
  A controlled, reproducible testbed for reduced-order modelling of
  particle-laden flow. Inertial particles in a prescribed unsteady vortical
  flow are converted into Eulerian concentration fields, compressed with POD
  and a convolutional autoencoder, and forecast in latent space with DMD and
  neural (MLP, Neural-ODE, GRU) models. Each model is compared against
  persistence and against the others, with results reported over training
  seeds and checked by a from-scratch re-run.
